Corrections (old -> new, why)
1. Islands "UZDoom has no map-wide grouping"; "Helion adds the map-wide level"; transfer row "Port/Rework, cull invalid in UZDoom"; feature row "island culling Helion-only" -> UZDoom has subsector_t::mapsection, computed by the same PartnerSeg flood (renderinfo.cpp:77-102), and a portal-aware viewer-section cull (hw_drawinfo.cpp:262-268, hw_bsp.cpp:696-697, hw_portal.cpp:668/808/915). Transfer grade changed to "(already present)"; intro and summary inference adjusted. Why: grep of UZDoom src for mapsection.
2. "UZDoom builds only when ForceNodeBuild is set or the node lumps are unusable" -> also builds GL nodes when shipped nodes are not GL-friendly (CheckNodes moves them to gamenodes, then loads cached/GWA nodes or builds). Caching only when build time >= gl_cachetime (0.6 s). Cites glnodes.cpp:921-984, g_cvars.cpp:39-40.
3. DECORATE "const" supported -> `const` throws "Variables not supported" exactly like `enum` (DecorateParser.cs:49-57). Added: a ParserException makes Parse return false and discards every actor in that lump (ParserBase.cs:68-73, DecorateDefinitions.cs:34-41).
4. TEXTURES "Supported (incl. component translations)" -> Partial: per-patch Translation/Flip/Rotate options are parsed but ArchiveImageRetriever composes using only Name+Offset (ArchiveImageRetriever.cs:133-148).
5. Translations row: "DECORATE Translation ranges and ICE ... cite DecoratePropertyParser.cs:130-143" -> :130-143 is Player.ColorRange. DECORATE `Translation` is parsed (:721-728, :1298) but Properties.Translation has no reader. TEXTURES component translations are not applied. ID24 TranslationEntry is applied (DefinitionEntries.cs:515-530).
6. ANIMDEFS "animated-door supported" -> ANIMATEDDOOR throws "not supported" (AnimatedDefinitions.cs:26-29). The exception is caught in ParseEntry, so the rest of that ANIMDEFS lump is skipped (DefinitionEntries.cs:265-281).
7. Teleport into closet "clears the flags" -> island flags are cleared, but the per-entity loop skips entities that have MonsterCloset set (inverted condition, WorldBase.cs:4202-4219), so monsters keep their flags. Transfer note updated.
8. Line "scratch counters (BlockmapCount, PhysicsCount) shared by render and physics" -> they are only reset (Line.cs:120-121); a grep finds no reader. The render/physics BlockmapCount uses are on Entity/Side/Island.
9. NEW finding: ZNODES non-fractional forms (XGLN/XGL2/ZGLN/ZGL2) pass Int16 splitters through MathHelper.FromFixed (/65536), ZNodesDefinition.cs:113-120. Those splitters would be mis-scaled. Added to node-format bullet, table row and open question (a).
10. "~3.6k-line BSP builder in Core/Maps/Bsp/**" -> ~3.0k. 3,588 is the whole directory, including the used GLBSP converter and zdbsp wrapper; the unused builder (BspBuilder + States + Geometry) is 2,980 lines.
11. ID24 UZDoom side "UMAPINFO id24 level number only" -> also enteranim/exitanim interlevel animations (umapinfo.cpp:63-64, wi_stuff.cpp:377-410) and id24.wad support loading (d_iwad.cpp:53). Still no ID24 Bits/SKYDEFS/GAMECONF/SBARDEF/TRAKINFO.
12. DECORATE implemented-function description -> added A_Stop and the Helion-specific A_FireRailGun. A_PlaySound uses DEH Misc1/Misc2 semantics and A_Explode is fixed 128/128; both ignore DECORATE args.
13. ZDoom specials unhandled list extended: LineAlign*, ThingDamage, ThingThrust, Hexen Stairs_Build*, Pillar_*, Ceiling_CrushRaiseAndStay*/CrushStay, ScrollWall, ScrollTextureBoth, LightStop (no handler outside LineSpecial.cs classification). Added Sector_Set3dFloor/TransferLight handling via == in InitSectors3D.
14. StructLine "refreshed only for the automap-seen flag" -> also MarkAutomap is toggled by MarkSpecials (MarkSpecials.cs:438-442). Noted that HasSpecial/teleport/exit bits are not refreshed when specials change.
15. Lump-reader absence claim "grep found nothing except A_CHECKTERRAIN" -> case-insensitive grep also hits the LockDefinitions class and commented-out ACS terrain functions. Added DefinitionEntries.cs:111-135 dispatch table as proof. LockDefinitions cite 11-34 -> 13-139 (whole constructor).
16. Physics blockmap "sorted by line id" -> sorted by block index, then line id (BlockLine.CompareTo).
17. Render blockmap row -> also holds per-cell render-entity heads (HeadRenderEntities).
18. BSP grid "each single cell stores the deepest node that wholly contains it" -> it stores the last node whose splitter did not cut the cell (one level above the first splitting node). Added inference: only the flat index is bounds-checked, so out-of-grid x wraps rows.
19. Sound "skips BadSubsectors listeners" -> sector-plane sound sources do not treat a listener in a BadSubsector as inside the sector.
20. Netplay grep: author's "none" holds only for socket/UdpClient/TcpClient/netgame; "multiplayer" matches item-stay and thing-flag code. Clarified.
21. Assets claim -> Assets/Assets/Actors is also Doom/Chex only.
22. StructLine consumers -> added sound propagation (WorldBase.cs:1001); renderer use is the line-heights buffer.

